**Convention 109.2 (literal traffic is not a Read count).** Use NLBAII
§65's exact codec: for reduced $q=n/d$, $d>0$, let
$\ell(q)=2\operatorname{bl}(|n|)+2\operatorname{bl}(d)+3$, with its
stated zero convention. A valid raw selector $j$ has length
$2\operatorname{bl}(j)+1$. The rational source-channel payload through
the dark cut of either *marker* run is exactly

$$
\sum_{i=1}^k\left[
3\ell(\theta_i)+2\ell(11\theta_i/2)+2\ell(3\theta_i/2)\right].
\tag{109.1}
$$

The two marker operands account for two copies of $\ell(\theta_i)$;
the actual assay reply accounts for the third. For a general-preparation
run replace its $2\sum_i\ell(\theta_i)$ marker term by
$\sum_{j=0}^{I}\sum_{v=1}^{b}\ell(h_{j,v}(x_\theta))$, where the
$h_j$ are its actually computed and submitted Construction 62.3 blocks.
Repair adds $\sum_{i\in J}\ell(\theta_i/2)$ for the chosen ports,
not an all-$k$ term when partial advice changes $J$. Inherited signs
have the same codec length. Selected use adds its actual operand and
reply payloads; requested reports add their own output payloads.

These formulas are only rational payloads. Add all actual selectors,
constructor addresses and replies, operation/refusal tags, ACKs, framing,
End, local acknowledgements, Return, owned producer ingress, $R\theta$
handoff, decoded reports, navigation and every inner/outward copy/export.
A literal designated germ exports $bM$ nonempty rational words even
when zero. Metric, source/predictor and Time exports have their actual
output sizes. A symbolic identity or one scalar reply does not make
those outputs free or supply an unperformed source assay.

